.prose
  :markdown
    # Query Objects

    The [Service Objects guide](#{guide_path("services")}) moves the
    *writes* out of your controllers and models. This guide does the same
    for the *reads*. A query object is a class that owns one model's
    non-trivial queries — the filtered listing, the search, the report —
    with typed, validated arguments and a description of what each query
    is for. We use [ActiveQuery](https://github.com/matiasasis/active-query)
    for it: a small DSL over ActiveRecord that returns ordinary relations,
    so everything you already know about chaining still applies.

