.mt-6.prose
  :markdown
    The line between the first two is *arguments and rules*. The moment a
    scope wants two parameters, a default, or a "but only when…", it is a
    query. The line between a query and an interaction is *side effects*:
    a query object must never write, enqueue, or send — if it needs to, it
    was an interaction all along, and the interaction can call the query
    for its reads.

